title The page that named half its directory
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment
think Standfast closed first: three guards red on the cold open, all three repaired and shipped as 9c59a9a852 with REDS %188. The line reopened, and the crux two laps have pointed at was image/README.md at 400,042 bytes.
think Measured before splitting rather than after. comm between ls image/*.rye and every `name.rye` the page cites read 112 named against 227 on disk, and two of the 112 -- dexter_line.rye and scooter_compose.rye -- name files that stand in pond/apps/, cited by bare name beside local ones so they read as if they lived here. So 117 modules had landed with nobody adding a line.
think The 117 are one arc rather than a scatter: threshold, label, regions, contour, chain_code, polygon, moments, hu_moments, skeleton, thin, zhang_suen, branch, endpoints, prune, medial_axis, distance, watershed, the convex family, the nine click_ gestures, the four lasso_ gestures, fourteen cluster_ modules and thirteen line_ modules. All of Season G's shape analysis, selection, and scene structure. Every one has a witness -- 248 *_witness.rish files across the tool rooms name a path under image/, 247 before this round's own -- so not one was unproven, only unlisted.
think This is REDS %184 at three and a half times the scale, in the directory %187's own ratchet had pointed at. The new half is a corollary: a page that names some of a directory is read as naming all of it, and the larger the page the more completely it is believed. At 400,042 bytes nobody was going to count.
think Took the Caravan shape rather than inventing one. The page splits into a Door front page and four pages beside it in the SAME directory, so every relative link inside the lifted prose stays true byte for byte -- which is why the lift is a move rather than a rewrite. The three sections came out at their original line ranges, their `###` headings demoted to `##`, and each new page carries a header naming what it is and where it came from.
think MODULES.md is the new writing. 227 rows in twelve families, each row `| [`name.rye`](name.rye) | what it does |`, and every sentence extracted from that module's own `//!` head comment rather than composed -- so the page says what the code says. The extraction handled two forms of doc head (`--` and the elder em-dash), stripped the `HUNKnn:` prefix, cut at the first clause boundary, dropped a fragment opened by an unmatched paren, and lowercased emphasis capitals while keeping RGBA, CSS, WCAG, HSL and the proper names Freeman, Sobel, Andrew, Zhang-Suen, Douglas-Peucker.
think The guard matches the Module column rather than any `.rye` link, which is the load-bearing choice Caravan's scan already paid for: the arc pages cite their own modules in prose constantly, and a reading that counted those would call a short table complete. Two readings are new here -- a name carrying digits binds its row, since forty-eight font5x7_ modules do, and a seam symlink counts as a module, since parse_int.rye and tally_copy.rye are what a reader finds in this directory.
think Proved the RED path on the real page rather than only in the pen: deleted the watershed.rye row and the scan read unrostered=1 verdict=roster_incomplete, naming the file; restored and it read bijection=yes at 227 of 227.
obs The meter bit my own repair on the lap it was written. The new Door page joined tools/fixtures/prose_register_scan.sh's DOOR roster and read 27% negative sentences against the 20% ceiling -- so I swept it to 13% with every claim held exactly: no-network-no-key became what a picture already has on your machine, the road not taken became one line undo and redo run along, never moved became moving money stays a hand's work, and never from the reference C became that spec is the whole of what we read. That is %185's rule working the first time it was given the chance, on the page it was written for.
obs The over-bound ratchet falls 7 to 6, and its control now plants six free and seven bitten rather than seven and eight. A ceiling that only falls is only true if the lap that earns the fall takes it.
obs Booking %189 carried the pin past its bound again, so row %185 folded to construction/archive/ with its three ../tools/ links deepened and the header's own left alone. Second fold of the day, same rule, no rediscovery.
obs Named and left for its own round: 21 .rye files in image/ carry non-ASCII in their doc comments, from before ASCII-first was seated. A mechanical sweep, and not this lap's work.
